In 1899 two men from Chattanooga got the rights to bottle Coca-Cola. They built the plants, Coca-Cola sold them the syrup. Within about 20 years there were 1,000+ bottling plants. Full documentary: {LONG}
Sources: The Coca-Cola Company history (The Asa Candler Era).
